WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.310
One photo.

2
00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.450
A volunteer in waders
pushes through floodwater,

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.160
carrying a small, soaked dog.

4
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.400
Drop it onto a newspaper page.

5
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.730
A plain headline appears above
it, and a calm caption below.

6
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.440
Now drop the same picture onto a poster.

7
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.010
A huge slogan, and a
button asking you to give.

8
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.020
Same dog.

9
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.260
Same water.

10
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.000
So why do the words change so much?

11
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.930
In this mission, you'll meet three
questions to ask of any text:

12
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.720
purpose, audience and form.

13
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.680
Is the report true,
and the advert made up?

14
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.970
You'll test that on two
texts about one flood.

15
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.680
And you'll read the layout too, from the
headline and caption to a web address.

16
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.440
Your mission: explain why
the words are so different.
